# AI Career OS – Career Page Template (Master Template)

## Purpose

This template is the official standard for every Career page inside AI Career OS.

Every career must follow this structure to ensure consistency in user experience, learning flow, design language, and scalability.

The goal is not to create an informational page, but to build an interactive AI-powered career workspace that guides users from beginner to job-ready.

---

# 1. Hero Section

Display the most important career information immediately.

Contents:

* Career Title
* Short Description (2–3 sentences)
* Career Category
* Difficulty Level
* Estimated Learning Time
* Average Salary
* Hiring Demand
* Remote Work Availability
* AI Compatibility Score
* "Start Learning" CTA

---

# 2. Career Snapshot

Quick overview dashboard.

Include:

* Hiring Demand
* Growth Rate
* Automation Risk
* Remote Opportunities
* AI Usage Level
* Market Trend
* Job Security
* Future Outlook

---

# 3. Career Overview

Explain:

* What this career is
* Main responsibilities
* Typical daily work
* Industries
* Companies that hire
* Why this career matters in the AI era

---

# 4. Is This Career Right For You?

### Good Fit If...

List personality traits and interests.

### Might Not Be Ideal If...

Mention common challenges honestly.

---

# 5. Career Roadmap

The heart of the page.

Each phase contains:

* Overview
* Learning Goals
* Courses
* Resources
* Practical Missions
* Notes
* Quiz
* Completion Status

Typical phases:

1. Foundations
2. Core Skills
3. Professional Tools
4. Real Projects
5. Portfolio
6. Job Preparation

---

# 6. Skills Required

Separate into:

Technical Skills

Soft Skills

Each skill includes:

* Importance
* Difficulty
* Progress Tracking

---

# 7. Tools & Software

Display:

* IDEs
* AI Tools
* Frameworks
* Platforms
* Cloud Services
* Productivity Tools

---

# 8. Learning Resources

Organize by:

Free Courses

Paid Courses

Books

Documentation

YouTube Channels

Blogs

Communities

Certificates

---

# 9. Hands-on Missions

Real practical tasks.

Organize as:

Beginner

Intermediate

Advanced

Expert

Capstone Project

---

# 10. Portfolio Projects

Projects employers like to see.

For each:

* Description
* Difficulty
* Skills Learned
* Estimated Time

---

# 11. Certifications

Recommended industry certifications.

Include:

* Provider
* Difficulty
* Cost
* Importance

---

# 12. AI Tools Used in This Career

Display tools commonly used by professionals.

Examples:

* ChatGPT
* Claude
* Gemini
* GitHub Copilot
* Cursor
* Perplexity
* OpenAI API

---

# 13. Career Progression

Visual roadmap.

Previous Careers

↓

Current Career

↓

Advanced Careers

Show possible transitions.

---

# 14. Salary & Job Market

Include:

Global Salary

Europe

USA

Germany

Remote

Job Growth

Market Demand

---

# 15. Daily Workflow

Timeline of a typical workday.

Example:

09:00 Planning

10:00 Development

11:30 Meetings

13:00 Project Work

15:00 Reviews

17:00 Documentation

---

# 16. Real-World Use Cases

Explain where professionals work.

Examples:

Startups

Enterprise

Freelancing

Consulting

Agencies

---

# 17. AI Mentor Tips

An AI mentor provides guidance throughout the roadmap.

Include:

Common mistakes

Learning shortcuts

Interview advice

Career tips

Best practices

---

# 18. Community

Useful communities.

Examples:

GitHub

LinkedIn

Discord

Reddit

Forums

---

# 19. FAQ

Answer common questions.

Target:

10–15 high-quality questions.

---

# 20. Related Careers

Recommend similar careers.

Display as interactive cards.

---

# 21. Personal Notes

Private notes section.

Users can:

* Add notes
* Edit notes
* Delete notes

Notes are saved automatically.

---

# 22. Progress Tracker

Track:

Completed Phases

Completed Courses

Projects

Quizzes

Portfolio

Career Readiness Score

---

# 23. Final Challenge

A comprehensive real-world project combining all learned skills.

Completion of this challenge indicates job readiness.

---

# Design Principles

Every Career page must be:

* Mobile-first
* Modern
* Clean
* Interactive
* Motivating
* AI-powered
* Easy to scan
* Easy to navigate
* Minimal scrolling where possible
* Performance optimized

---

# UX Principles

Every section should answer one question:

What is this career?

Why should I learn it?

How do I learn it?

How do I practice it?

How do I get hired?

How do I continue growing?

The page should feel like an AI Career Operating System rather than a traditional article.
